{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And better.</b> The word עדן is a compound and it is deficient, missing a heh before the nun and after it, like עדנה. The meaning is that the dead who have already died have found rest and have not heard the voice of a taskmaster, and they are better than the living and the dead who have not yet been created, because the oppressed in their bodies are like prisoners and captives, or the oppressed in money, who suffer. And if they are living, and the dead — if he is not now, he was already oppressed too. And many have wondered how he can say 'and better' of one who was not created. And so too the Sages, of blessed memory, said: happy is the one who was not created. And it is not surprising, on account of the brevity of language to speak thus, but rather by way of imaginings, as the masters of equal judgment say, for every thing is either yesh or ayin, and if it is a thing, how is it ayin."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Reading חכמי שקול הדעת ('masters of equal judgment'); the phrase is textually unusual and may reflect a technical philosophical term or a corrupt reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:28.278244021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}